# AI Review Rule

When the user asks to run, design, update, or inspect AI Review:

1. Read `AI-Review/README.md`, `AI-Review/DESIGN.md`, `AI-Review/IMPLEMENTATION.md`, `AI-Review/MODEL_PROTOCOL.md`, `AI-Review/CONFIG_REFERENCE.md`, and `.ai-review.yaml` first.
2. Prefer the `ai-review` CLI if available.
3. Do not directly modify original note text.
4. Only modify AI-Review managed folded blocks, issue files, Dashboard, and state files.
5. Do not show topic keywords in source note folded blocks.
6. Put topic keywords in issue frontmatter/body and Dashboard only.
7. Issue files must reference the source ReviewUnit block ID, for example `[[note.md#^ru000001]]`.
8. Issue IDs are never reused, never merged, and never shared across ReviewUnits.
9. Correct ReviewUnits do not get issue files.
10. Empty heading sections are skipped.
11. Sensitive API config belongs in `.ai-review-secrets.yaml`, not tracked files.

Managed block format:

```markdown
<!-- ai-review:start unit=ru000001 -->
> [!bug]- AI Review `ru000001`
> - [ ] [[AI-Review/Open/ar0001-Major-问题标题|ar0001]]
> `2026-05-04` · GPT-5.5/DeepSeek
<!-- ai-review:end -->
^ru000001
```
